-- title:
--   Finite extensions of ℚ_q come from number fields
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, write $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ for `PadicAlgCl q` (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$) and let $\iota_q =$ [`padicEmbedding q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L17) be the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` $\to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ obtained by lifting along algebraic closedness. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q$ which is finite-dimensional as a $\mathbb{Q}_q$-vector space. The assertion is that there exists an intermediate field $F$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$ and satisfies $K \le \mathbb{Q}_q\bigl(\iota_q(F)\bigr)$, the right-hand side being the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}_q$ by the image under $\iota_q$ of the underlying set of $F$. In words: every finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$ is contained in the completion-side field generated by the image of some number field.
--
--   This is the statement that the fields $\mathbb{Q}_q(\iota_q(F))$, with $F/\mathbb{Q}$ finite inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, are cofinal among the finite extensions of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q$; dually, the corresponding 'global levels' are cofinal among the open subgroups of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_q/\mathbb{Q}_q)$. It is used in the comparison of local and global Galois groups along $\iota_q$, for instance by [`exists_finiteDimensional_comap_localGaloisToGlobal_iff`](thm.html#exists_finiteDimensional_comap_localGaloisToGlobal_iff), by [`IntermediateField.isSolvable_algEquiv_of_padic`](thm.html#IntermediateField.isSolvable_algEquiv_of_padic) and in the place-decomposition material.
